l,"evidence":["gate_dispatch._attach_completion_metrics (gate_dispatch.py:684-687): '_sum_run_consumption returns None ... the block is OMITTED gracefully' — verdict['metrics'] is only set when an LLM step ran","completion_sidecar.py:329: metrics = v.get('metrics') if isinstance(v.get('metrics'), dict) else None — absence is expected and handled as None","A child-closure/deterministic-short-circuit FAIL produces a verdict with NO metrics key"],"finding":"The plan's stated merge target — the completion verdict's existing 'metrics' dictionary — is not guaranteed to exist on every verdict, so 'merge the direct fields into its existing metrics dictionary' has no dictionary to extend on a deterministic short-circuit verdict.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f180b7797407b9407","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section: 'Immediately after it returns, merge the direct fields into its existing metrics dictionary'; AC 'A model-backed FAIL COMPLETION_VERDICT carries all ten direct timing fields.'","norm_id":"ndce37aaa0c5602b0","priority":0.2513,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A FAIL verdict produced without an LLM run (deterministic short-circuit) has no metrics dict; merging into 'its existing metrics dictionary' would either no-op or need to create one, which the plan does not specify"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that the merge initializes verdict['metrics'] = {} when the key is missing before adding the timing fields, preserving any existing consumption metrics when present.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reach